  "scope": "For odd q=29,31,33,35,37,39 an exact crossing decomposition below q^sqrt(2) has at most four pieces. One, two, and three pieces are excluded by q^2, the all-field two-piece bound, and the three-piece cross relaxation. For four pieces, every piece has both ranks at least two and smaller rank at most floor(q^sqrt(2)-3q). Writing the larger rank L and smaller rank m, the quotient bound gives L<=q^2-f(m), and the two total-rank budgets fix the sums of L in the row-small and column-small groups. The checker enumerates every small-rank multiset and orientation partition, and minimizes the concave group costs at the bound vertices. All cases clear the target with margin >1. This is a finite cross-constraint closure, not a score change and not a claim for even q or q>=41.",
